    "b-ks2-path-runphase-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-runphase-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Closed worker states provide evidence for knowledge processing. With --worker-summary enabled, the summary processor schedules eligible ended runs. The summary job combines transcript reasoning with the deterministic run digest, persists worker_run and submission records, and enqueues a run_closed index task. The independently enabled --librarian-consumer researches those tasks and proposes evidence-backed changes. Both consumers default to off."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-runphase-intro-detail-1": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-runphase-intro-detail-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The host records integration outcomes deterministically. Conflicts persist as blocking outcomes with their evidence and conflict paths; they do not launch a resolver agent or guarantee automatic target requeue. An unsuccessful attempt can still supply useful knowledge when it is eligible for summarization. Librarian curation follows the current subject context and drift rules before proposals reach the apply layer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
